{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T19:24:01Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-132475-en",
  "_rev": "37hNSegHf4NtjSKr1qpnPg",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T16:12:39Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ic4vqkej9fve",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "em"
          ],
          "text": "Egypt doesn't really have a \"bad time.\" It has times that don't suit the trip you have in mind. The same month means something different at the pyramids, in "
        },
        {
          "_key": "l5212ypqtdup",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "em",
            "ikldq6gs0xu3"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "vaot1vwio9mb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "em"
          ],
          "text": ", on the Red Sea, and in the desert."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "ikldq6gs0xu3",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ljwv5uqfztt5",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The most common answer to the question of when to travel in Egypt is \"October to April.\" That is broadly right, especially for a first trip that goes through "
        },
        {
          "_key": "vmf4d1hgdbcs",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "dg72dwhz8er6"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "662ofrqhvc47",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "3q8xej27ag5w",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "qkl8a8dcbqgo"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "mqtboz503elq",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Luxor, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "5rk2oxks02e1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "5qpp08okf5k5"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "yvhlymbple9a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "6jcqwid1jy5i",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "u57l96i4bnae"
          ],
          "text": "Abu Simbel"
        },
        {
          "_key": "byp1vep9702j",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "dg72dwhz8er6",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "qkl8a8dcbqgo",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "5qpp08okf5k5",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "u57l96i4bnae",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "p2chrios0zr1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "But Egypt is large. The Mediterranean coast at "
        },
        {
          "_key": "wcpvg4v7iyy1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "9042aq0e7e5q"
          ],
          "text": "Alexandria"
        },
        {
          "_key": "7muz4sx1ry2o",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Cairo, the upper Egypt of Luxor and Aswan, the Red Sea at "
        },
        {
          "_key": "oi4a7yzooqty",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "9it6ywepp486"
          ],
          "text": "Hurghada"
        },
        {
          "_key": "jn9ycj3aac7c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and Sharm, and the oases of the Western Desert do not share the same season. A summer in Luxor is severe; a summer beach holiday on the Red Sea works. A winter desert is beautiful; the nights are cold."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "9042aq0e7e5q",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58750",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "9it6ywepp486",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "So the better way to choose is to decide first what the trip is centred on."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a first trip to Egypt"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a first trip built around Cairo, Giza, Luxor, and Aswan, November, February, and March are particularly easy."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "November settles the heat and is less crowded than the winter peak. The pyramids and Luxor both walk well and the Nile cruise season is open."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "February sits after the Christmas–New Year crush, with good temperatures and strong upper-Egypt site work. If the Abu Simbel sun alignment matters to you, planning around 22 February is an option."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "March warms a little but still travels easily. Spring carries the khamsin wind, which on some days throws dust and can disrupt outdoor sightseeing."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The most comfortable stretch: October to April"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "October to April is the base travel season for Egypt's main destinations. To run Cairo, Giza, Luxor, and Aswan without strain, choose inside this range."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "October still carries summer heat early in the month and travels better the closer you get to the end. November is one of the most reliable months. December and January are strong on weather and the most crowded; prices climb. February balances well. March and April mix spring warmth and a little instability."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Late December into early January carries heavy international travel; popular hotels and Nile cruises fill early. If you go then, book early and prioritise early-morning sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor and Aswan"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "w5gx5tf1khxz",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor and Aswan are the most weather-sensitive places to choose for. Summer is genuinely hot, and walking the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "hez5dnbobw0x",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "v1bk3xsiguav"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Kings"
        },
        {
          "_key": "2slbs8yvpez6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and Karnak takes a real toll."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "v1bk3xsiguav",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The best window is November through March. Morning sites are pleasant and afternoons read well from the boat or the hotel. April is workable, with heat building in the second half. Late October is also a good choice."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Upper Egypt from May to September is cheaper and quieter, but the heat is the cost. To go in summer, rework the day: sites only in the early morning, midday rest, shade and water as non-negotiables."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo and Giza"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo and Giza are not as extreme as Luxor, but the summer is hot and spring can be hit by khamsin."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To walk the pyramids comfortably, November through March is the easy range. Winter mornings are cool, and evenings can be colder than you expect — bring a light layer in winter."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Spring on clear days is beautiful; on a dust day, visibility drops and outdoor sightseeing wears you down. Built-in margin in the schedule reduces the impact of those days."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Red Sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "p64f7hjek4rh",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hurghada, Sharm el-Sheikh, and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "jpr7njcwt6tg",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "vs4mohbpl6rp"
          ],
          "text": "Marsa Alam"
        },
        {
          "_key": "6uwijuplxfzo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " run on a different calendar from the sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "vs4mohbpl6rp",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58885",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For beach and snorkelling, October to May is the most comfortable. Not too hot, the water is enjoyable, and resort stays work."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Summer on the Red Sea is also possible. There is heat, but the trip works if it is built around the water. If you spend the day in the pool or the sea and don't add much land sightseeing, summer is a real option."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Combining the Red Sea and Luxor in the same summer trip needs care. The sea may be easy; the inland sites are a different heat entirely."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Western Desert and the oases"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa, Bahariya, the White Desert, Dakhla, Kharga — autumn through spring is the time. October to March is the season."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Winter desert days walk well; the nights are cold. For camping, bring warmth. Places like the White Desert read most beautifully in winter, when the low-angle light brings the rock forms forward."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A summer Western Desert trip is not recommended. Heat is severe and the risk of vehicle trouble or health problems goes up. If the desert is the centre of the trip, pick a cool season."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Alexandria and the north coast"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Alexandria and the Mediterranean coast carry a slightly different seasonal sense. Summer fills with domestic travellers escaping Cairo's heat, and the town's coastal character comes forward."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For quiet sightseeing, spring or autumn is better. Summer has life, but it crowds. Winter brings rain and wind days, with weather closer to the Mediterranean than the rest of Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "On Ramadan"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ramadan moves date each year. It affects travel, but it isn't a season to rule out."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "During the day, some shops and restaurants change hours, and in more local areas, eating and drinking openly calls for care. After sunset, the city comes strongly alive — iftar, family gatherings, the energy of the night — and carries a particular air."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The main sites generally remain open. Transfers, meals, and opening hours simply need a more flexible handling. If you travel during Ramadan, don't pack the days; leave room for the night side of Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Month-by-month at a glance"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "January is cool and comfortable, but the first week is crowded. February balances very well. March is warm and suits spring travel, with dust days to watch for. April is still good; the second half warms up."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "May is when crowds begin to thin and prices can soften, but upper Egypt gets hot. June through August is for the Red Sea; for site travel in Luxor and Aswan it is severe. September is hot in the first half and starts to travel more easily in the second."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "October is better late in the month, and November is one of the most reliable months of the year. December has good weather and the Christmas and year-end crowd."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Finally"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a first trip to ancient Egypt: November, February, March. For a Red Sea rest: October to May, or a dedicated summer beach trip. For the desert: October to March. For going deep in Luxor and Aswan, skip high summer."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters in choosing the season is not average temperature alone. Where you walk, what hour you move, how crowded it will be, what the city looks like at night. Choosing with all of that in view makes Egypt much easier to travel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
  "category": {
    "_ref": "wp-category-360",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "deck": "The best time to visit Egypt depends on where you're going. Cairo, Luxor, Aswan, the Red Sea, and the Western Desert each have their own season.",
